  "strategy": "**1. Approach and rationale**\n\nWe aim to minimize the Erdos minimum overlap constant \\(C_5\\) by optimizing a step function \\(h(x)\\) over \\([0, 2]\\) with integral 1. The minimization involves reducing the dimension by one variable through the integral constraint, ensuring feasible solutions by embedding the parent solution as a fallback. We employ a global-local strategy with:\n\n- **Random sampling** of initial points in the reduced \\(41\\)-dimensional space\n- **GA for coarse exploration** to escape local optima\n- **Polynomial interpolation** for local refinement near promising points\n- **Constraint handling** through fixed-parameter embedding for integral condition\n\nThis approach enhances sample diversity and leverages function evaluation results to generate better neighbors, addressing the high dimensionality and non-convexity of the optimization problem.\n\n**2. Mathematical specification**\n\nWe parameterize a \\(42\\)-point \\(h\\) vector (\\(n_{\\text{points}} = 42\\)):\n\n- \\(h \\in \\mathbb{R}^{42}\\) with \\(0 \\leq \\sum h_i = 21\\)\n- Variable reduction reduces dimension by one: \\(y_i = h_{i}\\) for \\(i=0\\) to \\(40\\)\n- The last variable \\(h_{41} = 21 - \\sum_{i=0}^{40} y_i\\) ensuring integral constraint\n- Feasibility requires \\(0 \\leq y_{i} \\leq 1\\) and \\(20 \\leq \\sum_{i=0}^{40} y_i \\leq 21\\)\n\nObjective: minimize \\(C_5 = \\max_k {\\rm{overlap}}\\{k\\}\\) where:\n\\[\nC_5 = \\max_k \\frac{2}{42} \\cdot | \\{ i : 0 \\leq x_i < 2 \\text{ and } 0 \\leq x_i + k < 2 \\} |\n\\]\nscalars \\(x_i\\).\n\nConstraints are enforced through fixed-parameter embedding, bounds, and complementarity checking.\n\n**3. Implementation procedure**\n\n- **Parent validation**: Verify initial_h_values has \\(0 \\leq h_i \\leq 1\\) and sum \\(= 21\\)\n- **Build objective function**: Compute max overlap for \\(42\\)-point vector, handles fixed-parameter contraction\n- **GA implementation** with fitness \\(-\\ln C_5\\) to maximize minimization\n- **Polynomial interpolation** for local search around top individuals\n- **Repair mechanism**: Clamp values to bounds and adjust sum to \\(20-21\\) range for feasibility\n\nComponents:\n\n- **objective_function**(\\(y\\)): Uses fixed-parameter condition \\(h= y \\oplus [21 - \\sum y]_{\\text{clamped}}\\) and computes max correlation\n- **objective_gradient**(\\(y\\)): Optional finite-difference gradient estimation\n- **f_constraint**(\\(y\\)): Integral feasibility check\n- **bound_clamp**: Enforces \\(0 \\leq y_i \\leq 1\\)\n- **polynomial_refinement**: Takes three best points and fits \\(p(t) = a t^2 + b t + c\\) then interpolates\n\n**4. Search choices and variations**\n\n- **Core GA**: Binary tournament selection, DE crossover, polynomial mutation\n- **Mixed strategy**: Run GA population for global search, then interpolate near top individual\n- **Parameter adaptation** in mutation rate \\([0.1, 0.3]\\) based on diversity\n- **Diversity maintenance** via epsilon elite strategy (keep worst \\(20\\%\\) for diversity)\n\n**5. Compute budget and robustness**\n\n- **Time estimate**: 5000-10000 function evaluations \\(\\times 0.1\\) seconds/eval \\(\\approx 500-1000\\) seconds\n- **Fallback**: Return parent solution if no valid candidate found\n- **Termination** when \\(1100\\) seconds exceed or GA stagnation occurs\n\n**6. Validation and return contract**\n\n- **Feasibility checks**: Ensure \\(0 \\leq h_i \\leq 1\\), sum \\(= 21\\)\n- **Recompute objective** with candidate to confirm evaluation\n- **Final output**: Validates feasibility, rechecks constraints at final solution",
